om/godotengine/godot/pull/123103.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-07T21:26:47Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCorrect the documentation's explanation of the smoothing curve. For non-empty ranges, the interpolation is slowest at the beginning and end of the range, and fastest halfway through.\r\nAlign the C# return behavior when the range is empty (`from == to`) with Godot Core / GDScript.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThe documentation is based on the existing Core / GDScript documentation:\r\n[doc/classes/@GlobalScope.xml](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/doc/classes/%40GlobalScope.xml)\r\n\r\nThe C# implementation now matches the existing Core behavior:\r\n[core/math/math_funcs.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/math/math_funcs.h)\r\n\r\n## Testing \r\nBuilt Godot with C# support and compiled GodotSharp.\r\nRan a local C# runtime test covering the float and double empty-range cases, positive and negative ranges. All checks passed.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godot